    "updated_at": "2019-10-15T15:30:54Z",
    "body": "as much as i'm not a fan of `accesskey` and would not shed a tear if it actually disappeared altogether, i could imagine the first press of the key going to the *first* element in source order/tree hierarchy with that `accesskey` getting focus (similar to what happens with things like multiple elements with the same `id` and doing a `document.getElementById`). beyond that, it *could* be an idea that on pressing the same key again, the browser cycles to the next one in order? so something similar to a tab cycle?",
