    "created_at": "2022-10-27T01:08:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-27T01:08:34Z",
    "body": "> Blink / WebKit seems to ~focus~ _activate_ the last element […],\r\n> Firefox focus the first such an element […].\r\n\r\nIt seems WebKit's behaviour has changed and diverged from Blink, to now favour the first element instead of the last.\r\n\r\nTest case: <https://codepen.io/Krinkle/pen/KKewZMW?editors=1000>\r\n\r\nUnique accesskey X:\r\n* Firefox: activate X.\r\n* Safari: activate X.\r\n* Chromium: activate X.\r\n\r\nDuplicate accesskey X Y Z:\r\n* Firefox: focus X, first.\r\n* Safari: activate X, first.\r\n* Chromium: activate Z, last.\r\n\r\nDuplicate accesskey X Y Z when only Y is visible:\r\n* Firefox: focus Y, first visible.\r\n* Safari: activate X, any first.\r\n* Chromium: activate Z, any last.\r\n",
